cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Plasticity Frontier: Preparing zero-output networks for one-step learning"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/plasticity-frontier"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/plasticity-frontier"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for preparing zero-output deep linear networks under joint
  initialization-norm and trainable-parameter budgets. Estimates task structure,
  solves constrained update-map problems, compiles the maps into network weights,
  and checks the simultaneous first gradient step. In a controlled Gaussian
  experiment across 31 independent source preparations, joint selection reduced
  mean conditional coefficient error from 0.754794 to 0.706105, a descriptive
  reduction of 6.45 percent. Direct operators reproduce the network updates;
  empirical Bayes achieves lower error in a separate fixed-cohort comparison.
  Includes plotting data, exact rational fixtures and a matched same-machine
  clean-replay receipt. Broader practical or nonlinear-network advantage is unproved.
keywords:
  - initialization
  - learning geometry
  - deep linear networks
  - one-step learning
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: report
    title: "The cost of preparing a network to learn: A sharp norm formula for zero-output deep linear networks and an isotropic-to-specialized adaptation transition"
    authors:
      - name: "An autonomous mathematical investigation"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/plasticity-frontier/blob/main/docs/prepared_learning_research.pdf"
